From: Kettle <kettle@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:17:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] rauc post-install: run the hooks in post-install.d

Executables in $libdir/rauc/post-install.d/ run with the updated slot's
name once it is installed and marked for its first boot, so a distribution
can add steps (Kettle Linux: its bootloaders that can't choose a slot) without
patching this script. A failing hook is a warning, not a failed update.
---
 atomic-update/rauc/post-install.sh.in | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/atomic-update/rauc/post-install.sh.in b/atomic-update/rauc/post-install.sh.in
index ead2cfb..665bcec 100755
--- a/atomic-update/rauc/post-install.sh.in
+++ b/atomic-update/rauc/post-install.sh.in
@@ -293,6 +293,16 @@ fi
 # attempts and setting it as the highest priority
 (( ERR == 0 )) && holo-bootconf --image $UPDATED_SLOT set-mode first-boot
 
+# Distribution hooks, run with the updated slot's name once it's installed and bootable.
+# The update stands even if one of them fails.
+if (( ERR == 0 )); then
+    for hook in @libdir@/rauc/post-install.d/*; do
+        [ -x "$hook" ] || continue
+        log "Running $hook $UPDATED_SLOT"
+        "$hook" "$UPDATED_SLOT" || warn "$hook failed"
+    done
+fi
+
 # Store the installed update version in a temporary file to record that we
 # have a pending reboot to switch to the new image
 # Additionally, record the current booted slot in a temporary file that
